NOW THEREFORE, in consideration of the terms and conditions hereinafter set out, the parties hereby agree as follows:

2. Definitions
“Affiliate" with respect to any person to which it refers, a person or entity that directly or indirectly through one or more intermediates, controls or is controlled by, or is under common control with, such subject person or entity. The term "control" includes, without limitation, the possession, directly or indirectly, of the power to direct or cause the direction of the management or policies of a person or entity, whether through the ownership of voting securities, by contract or otherwise.
“Confidential Information” shall mean nonpublic, proprietary or confidential information of either Party in whatever form, regarding business plans, financial data, operational data, product development plans, pricing, Intellectual Property, and other non‐public business info, whether identified as confidential information or not. Confidential Information shall also include the terms of this Agreement, Purchase Orders to be issued in accordance with this Agreement, and all documents and information released by either Party when performing its obligations under this Agreement.
“Distributor” shall have the meaning ascribed to such term in the preamble.
"Party", individually or "Parties", collectively shall mean each of Company and the Distributor (as hereafter defined).
“Product” shall mean the Products manufactured by the Company and as defined in clause 2.
“Intellectual Property” shall mean any patent, copyright, industrial design, trademark, trade name or other industrial or intellectual property right in respect of the Products and applications for any of the foregoing, for which Company and its Affiliates have the ownership rights or other rights, privileges, entitlements, and interests.
“Term” shall mean the duration of this Agreement in accordance with the provisions of Section 11 hereunder.
“Agreement” means this Agreement between Distributor and Company for the purpose of distribution of Product.
“Introduced Client” means any legal entity introduced by the Distributor to the Company in writing, including email, where the Distributor provides at least the client’s name, contact person, and basic project information.
“Protected Client” means any Introduced Client for which the Distributor has provided written notification to the Company.
“Protected Project” means any PV, hybrid or BESS project introduced by the Distributor between 1 January 2025 and 31 December 2027.
“Introduced Client Registry” means the internal registry maintained by the Distributor under Section [Client Introduction Registry].
“Penalty Fee” means the liquidated damages payable under Section [Anti-Circumvention Penalty Fee].

3. Client Introduction Registry
Section X – Client Introduction Registry
X.1 Distributor shall maintain an Introduced Client Registry and shall notify Company in writing (email sufficient) within five (5) Business Days of the Distributor’s first substantive contact with any potential client.
X.2 Each notification shall include:
(a) client’s legal name and registration number;
(b) contact person and title;
(c) project type (PV/hybrid/BESS) and estimated size;
(d) estimated budget;
(e) date of first contact.
X.3 The client becomes a Protected Client upon Distributor’s email notification, irrespective of Company acknowledgment.
X.4 Company shall not contact, negotiate with, quote to, or contract with any Protected Client without Distributor’s prior written consent (email sufficient).


4. Anti-Circumvention Penalty Fee
Section Y – Anti-Circumvention Penalty Fee
Y.1 If any member of the Company Group enters into direct or indirect contact, negotiation, quotation, tender, proposal, LOI, purchase order, supply agreement, EPC agreement, service agreement, or any other commercial activity (“Circumventing Transaction”) with any Protected Client or regarding any Protected Project without Distributor’s written consent (email sufficient), this constitutes circumvention.
Y.2 Penalty Fee (Liquidated Damages) Structure:
(a) Contract value ≤ €500,000: €75,000
(b) €500,001–€2,000,000: 15 percent of total contract value
(c) > €2,000,000: 20 percent of total contract value (capped at €500,000)
Y.3 Minimum Penalty Fee: €50,000 per violation.
Y.4 Each Circumventing Transaction is treated as a separate and cumulative breach.
Y.5 Payment due within thirty (30) days of Distributor’s written notice.
Y.6 Penalty Fee shall be due and payable subject to the condition that the Distributor has previously requested the Company to cease the infringements specified in Y1, and the Company has not ceased the infringements within 7 days from such notice and is enforceable independently and is not subject to any limitation of liability.

5. Appointment & Distributor Rights
Distributor is appointed as Official Hybrid/BESS Channel Partner for Cyprus, responsible for coordinating all feasibility studies, BESS sizing, engineering visits, EMS/PCS configuration, and hybridisation work together with Linyang HQ, however Distributor shall act as the intermediary in the conclusion of contracts between Linyang/Solarfun Poland and potential Clent.

6. Year-1 Sales Targets
Section – Sales Targets
T.1 Year-1: No minimum sales target, no minimum stock, no minimum purchase obligations.
T.2 Company may not terminate or restrict Distributor’s rights based on Year-1 performance.
T.3 Year-2 and Year-3 targets shall only be effective if mutually agreed in writing after Year-1 review.

7. Non-Competition
Section Z – Mutual Distribution Rights
Z.1 Distributor Rights and Obligations: Distributor may be entitled to distribute other BESS brands while ofering Linyang products a fair opportunity to compete and maintaining separation of technical and pricing materials.
Z.2 Company Exclusivity: Company shall not appoint any other distributor, agent, reseller or representative in Cyprus during the Term and for twenty-four (24) months following termination, except termination of the agreement due to the Distributor's failure to achieve target set up in written annex and in case of for material breach of agreement. For material breach of contract shall be consider a lack of sufficient activity required from Distributor according to this agreement by the Distributor.
Z.3 Release from Non-Compete: If Company appoints another Cyprus distributor, Distributor is automatically released from all non-compete obligations.

8. Payment Terms
Section P – Terms of Payment
P.1 Distributor’s payment obligations follow the end-client milestone schedule.
P.2 Any delay in end-client payments automatically extends Distributor’s payment deadline.
P.3 No penalties, interest, shipment suspension or termination may arise due to end-client delay.
P.4 Distributor shall notify Company of expected delays and provide reasonable supporting details.

9. Pricing Structure
New Appendix A – Pricing Structure
Base Price List for Cyprus to be provided within thirty (30) days.
Distributor discount: 20 percent off list price.
Volume discount: 2–5 percent for projects > €1M.
Price validity: 90 days.
Price adjustments only if:
Raw material costs change by >10% (verified)
EUR/CNY fluctuates by >8%
60 days advance notice
Applies only to new orders
Prices quoted in EUR, payments in EUR or USD (ECB rate).
Distributor free to set resale prices.

10. Termination
Section R – Termination
R.1 Agreement term: three (3) years, renewable.
R.2 Years 1–2: Termination for Cause Only. Company may terminate only for material breach, subject to a 90-day cure period.
R.3 Year 3+: Termination on Notice. Either party may terminate with 180-day written notice.
R.4 Market performance or sales volume is not grounds for termination.
R.5 Early Termination Compensation. If Company terminates without reason provided in agreement  before the end of Year-3:
(a) €100,000
(b) 25% of Distributor’s average gross profit over the past 12 months
(c) All outstanding revenues on ongoing projects
(d) Any Penalty Fees arising from Company contact with Introduced Clients within 24 months post-termination

11. Post-Termination Protections
Section S – Survival and Post-Termination Protections
The following survive termination until 31 December 2027:
(a) Introduced Client & Protected Project rights
(b) Anti-circumvention obligations
(c) Penalty Fee
(d) Confidentiality of client/project information
(e) No direct or indirect contracting with Protected Clients without Distributor consent
This clause may be amended only by written agreement signed by all Parties.


